---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../lib/ui';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, MIN_AGE, TERMS_UPDATED, TERMS_VERSION, contactHref } from '../lib/terms';

const mailto = contactHref();
---

<Layout title="Terms" description={`The terms for using ${SITE_NAME}, a free hobby site for playing Hearts.`}>
  <div class="container page" style="max-width: 760px">
    <div class="page-head">
      <div class="stack" style="--gap: 8px">
        <span class="eyebrow">Terms of use</span>
        <h1 class="display">The rules of the house</h1>
        <p class="muted lede">The card rules are on the <a href="/rules">How to play</a> page. These are the rules for using the site itself.</p>
        <p class="faint small">Version {TERMS_VERSION} · Updated {TERMS_UPDATED}</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <article class="stack doc" style="--gap: 20px">
      <section class="panel panel-pad">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>{SITE_NAME} is a free hobby project. It comes as-is, with no promises, and it might change or close.</li>
          <li>Be kind, don’t break things, and never play for real money.</li>
          <li>What you post stays yours, but you let us show it to the other players.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="muted">The rest of this page says the same thing at more length. By creating an account or using the site, you agree to all of it.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel panel-pad">
        <h2>Who runs this</h2>
        <p>
          {SITE_NAME} (“the site”) is run as a personal, non-commercial hobby. “We” and “us” mean the people who run it. It’s
          not a business, and nobody is paid to keep it running. If you don’t agree to these terms, please don’t use the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel panel-pad">
        <h2>No warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The site is free and provided <strong>“as is” and “as available”</strong>, without warranties of any kind, whether
          express or implied. That includes any warranty that it’s fit for a particular purpose, that it will always be up,
          that it’s free of bugs, or that games, scores and stats will never be lost.
        </p>
        <p>Features can change or disappear, and the whole site may shut down at any time, with or without notice.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel panel-pad">
        <h2>Limits on liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent the law allows, the people who run the site and anyone who helps them are not liable for any
          indirect, incidental, special, consequential or punitive damages, or for lost data, lost games or lost bragging
          rights, however they come about. If we’re found liable for something anyway, the most we’ll owe you in total is
          US$10.
        </p>
        <p>
          If someone makes a claim against us because of something you posted or did on the site against these terms, you
          agree to take responsibility for it.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">Some places don’t allow some of these limits. Where that’s the case, they apply as far as the law allows.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel panel-pad">
        <h2>Playing fair</h2>
        <p>When you use the site, please don’t:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>harass, bully, threaten or demean anyone;</li>
          <li>post anything illegal, hateful or sexually explicit, or anything you don’t have the right to share;</li>
          <li>pretend to be someone you’re not (the cats are allowed to be cats);</li>
          <li>
            attack the site: try to break in, get into accounts or games that aren’t yours, get around its limits, or overload
            it;
          </li>
          <li>scrape it, or play or collect data with bots or scripts of your own;</li>
          <li>
            use it for <strong>real-money gambling</strong>: no betting on games, no stakes, no cash prizes. The points are
            worth bragging rights and nothing else.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="panel panel-pad">
        <h2>Your account</h2>
        <p>
          Keep your password to yourself, and use one account per person. You’re responsible for what happens on your account.
          If you think someone else has been using it, let us know.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel panel-pad">
        <h2>Your content</h2>
        <p>
          Your display name, the names you give games, your profile photo and anything else you post (such as chat, if the site
          gets it) stay <strong>yours</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          By posting them, you give us a free, non-exclusive, worldwide permission to store them, copy them as needed to run the
          site, and show them to other players. That lasts while they’re on the site, and for a short time afterwards in
          backups.
        </p>
        <p>
          You must have the right to post what you post. Use a photo of yourself, or one you have permission to use. We may
          remove anything that breaks these terms.
        </p>
        <p>
          You’re responsible for what you post. Nobody reviews it before other players see it, and we’re not responsible for
          what other players post.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel panel-pad">
        <h2>Suspending and removing accounts</h2>
        <p>
          We can suspend, limit or remove any account or content that breaks these terms or puts the site or other players at
          risk. We may do this without warning. You can stop using the site whenever you like.
          The <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how to have your account deleted.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel panel-pad">
        <h2>Age</h2>
        <p>
          You must be at least <strong>{MIN_AGE}</strong> to create an account. If you’re under 18, or under the age of
          adulthood where you live, check with a parent or guardian first. We’ll remove any account we learn belongs to someone
          under {MIN_AGE}.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel panel-pad">
        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms or the Privacy Policy. When a change matters, the version number above goes up, and
          you’ll be asked to agree again the next time you open the site. If you don’t agree to the new version, please stop
          using the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel panel-pad">
        <h2>The legal bits</h2>
        <p>
          If part of these terms can’t be enforced, the rest still applies. If we don’t enforce something straight away, we
          haven’t given up the right to. These terms and the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> are the whole agreement
          between you and us about the site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel panel-pad">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms? {mailto ? <>Email us at <a href={mailto}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</> : 'Ask a site admin, or whoever invited you to the site.'}
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: 17px;
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  .small {
    font-size: 13.5px;
  }

  .doc {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .doc section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .doc h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 560;
    font-size: 22px;
  }

  .doc p,
  .doc li {
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .doc ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 6px;
  }
</style>
